river Account (role check)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>544d07d9-cb53-40b4-b25c-8df548357be5</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>2718b34a-c9ae-4b5b-8c60-020c6bd33cf4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E6544d07d9-cb53-40b4-b25c-8df548357be5bcb6fa45-f2e6-4997-936d-6df09b0783b92718b34a-c9ae-4b5b-8c60-020c6bd33cf4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f9cfa17b-9098-466d-94a6-c2c5c8cfa594</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>bcb6fa45-f2e6-4997-936d-6df09b0783b9</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>250</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>544d07d9-cb53-40b4-b25c-8df548357be5:bcb6fa45-f2e6-4997-936d-6df09b0783b9:2718b34a-c9ae-4b5b-8c60-020c6bd33cf4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>2.3 Assign Delivery to Driver  May be Subject to Elevation of Privilege Using Remote Code Execution</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>users.dat  may be able to remotely execute code for 2.3 Assign Delivery to Driver .</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Read Driver Account (role check)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>544d07d9-cb53-40b4-b25c-8df548357be5</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>2718b34a-c9ae-4b5b-8c60-020c6bd33cf4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>E7544d07d9-cb53-40b4-b25c-8df548357be5bcb6fa45-f2e6-4997-936d-6df09b0783b92718b34a-c9ae-4b5b-8c60-020c6bd33cf4</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f9cfa17b-9098-466d-94a6-c2c5c8cfa594</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>bcb6fa45-f2e6-4997-936d-6df09b0783b9</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>251</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>544d07d9-cb53-40b4-b25c-8df548357be5:bcb6fa45-f2e6-4997-936d-6df09b0783b9:2718b34a-c9ae-4b5b-8c60-020c6bd33cf4</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation by Changing the Execution Flow in 2.3 Assign Delivery to Driver </a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Elevation Of Privilege</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>A user subject gains increased capability or privilege by taking advantage of an implementation bug.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An attacker may pass data into 2.3 Assign Delivery to Driver  in order to change the flow of program execution within 2.3 Assign Delivery to Driver  to the attacker's choosing.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Read Driver Account (role check)</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>544d07d9-cb53-40b4-b25c-8df548357be5</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>2718b34a-c9ae-4b5b-8c60-020c6bd33cf4</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>E7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S76260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef80e625a7-0042-4f9d-944b-521701906dfa0ced8787-79d0-4908-a57a-f27aecb3f2d9</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f9cfa17b-9098-466d-94a6-c2c5c8cfa594</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>80e625a7-0042-4f9d-944b-521701906dfa</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>252</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>6260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef:80e625a7-0042-4f9d-944b-521701906dfa:0ced8787-79d0-4908-a57a-f27aecb3f2d9</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of Source Data Store shipments.dat </a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>shipments.dat  may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to incorrect data delivered to 2.4 Update Delivery Status (Dispatcher) . Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value> Shipment Record</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>6260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>0ced8787-79d0-4908-a57a-f27aecb3f2d9</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>S7</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>R66260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef80e625a7-0042-4f9d-944b-521701906dfa0ced8787-79d0-4908-a57a-f27aecb3f2d9</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f9cfa17b-9098-466d-94a6-c2c5c8cfa594</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>80e625a7-0042-4f9d-944b-521701906dfa</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>253</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>6260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef:80e625a7-0042-4f9d-944b-521701906dfa:0ced8787-79d0-4908-a57a-f27aecb3f2d9</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Potential Data Repudiation by 2.4 Update Delivery Status (Dispatcher) </a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Repudiation threats involve an adversary denying that something happened.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>2.4 Update Delivery Status (Dispatcher)  claims that it did not receive data from a source outside the trust boundary. Consider using logging or auditing to record the source, time, and summary of the received data.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value> Shipment Record</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>6260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>0ced8787-79d0-4908-a57a-f27aecb3f2d9</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>R6</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>I236260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef80e625a7-0042-4f9d-944b-521701906dfa0ced8787-79d0-4908-a57a-f27aecb3f2d9</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f9cfa17b-9098-466d-94a6-c2c5c8cfa594</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>80e625a7-0042-4f9d-944b-521701906dfa</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>254</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>6260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef:80e625a7-0042-4f9d-944b-521701906dfa:0ced8787-79d0-4908-a57a-f27aecb3f2d9</b:Interacti