c_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>D560fc2117-4f2f-4797-a79b-cd2329fc5a6c711cc6d4-936d-4401-80f8-cd226e0b85f96260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f9cfa17b-9098-466d-94a6-c2c5c8cfa594</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>711cc6d4-936d-4401-80f8-cd226e0b85f9</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>266</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>60fc2117-4f2f-4797-a79b-cd2329fc5a6c:711cc6d4-936d-4401-80f8-cd226e0b85f9:6260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Data Store Inaccessible</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Denial Of Service</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Denial of Service happens when the process or a datastore is not able to service incoming requests or perform up to spec.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>An external agent prevents access to a data store on the other side of the trust boundary.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value>Delivery Status</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>60fc2117-4f2f-4797-a79b-cd2329fc5a6c</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><b:TargetGuid>6260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef</b:TargetGuid><b:Title i:nil="true"/><b:TypeId>D5</b:TypeId><b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded><b:UserThreatCategory i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatDescription i:nil="true"/><b:UserThreatShortDescription i:nil="true"/><b:Wide>false</b:Wide></a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB><a:Key>S76260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6befc3176066-6c4f-4453-ac69-4abd70aa0efd60fc2117-4f2f-4797-a79b-cd2329fc5a6c</a:Key><a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase"><b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/><b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>f9cfa17b-9098-466d-94a6-c2c5c8cfa594</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid><b:FlowGuid>c3176066-6c4f-4453-ac69-4abd70aa0efd</b:FlowGuid><b:Id>267</b:Id><b:InteractionKey>6260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef:c3176066-6c4f-4453-ac69-4abd70aa0efd:60fc2117-4f2f-4797-a79b-cd2329fc5a6c</b:InteractionKey><b:InteractionString i:nil="true"/><b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt><b:Priority>High</b:Priority><b:Properties><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Title</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing of Source Data Store shipments.dat </a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatShortDescription</a:Key><a:Value>Spoofing is when a process or entity is something other than its claimed identity. Examples include substituting a process, a file, website or a network address.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key><a:Value>shipments.dat  may be spoofed by an attacker and this may lead to incorrect data delivered to 2.5 Update Delivery Status (Driver) . Consider using a standard authentication mechanism to identify the source data store.</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>InteractionString</a:Key><a:Value> Shipment Record</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:KeyValueOfstringstring><a:Key>Priority</a:Key><a:Value>High</a:Value></a:KeyValueOfstringstring></b:Properties><b:SourceGuid>6260a99f-7361-44eb-9ad4-805c568f6bef</b:SourceGuid><b:State>AutoGenerated</b:State><b:StateInformation i:nil="true"/><